  "creative_brief": {
    "question": "How does staying awake for 248 days shut down all four generators at once?",
    "answer": "A software counter in each generator control unit overflows at the same moment, and the failsafe cuts all AC power.",
    "proof": "FAA airworthiness directive 2015-10066: 248-day counter overflow, simultaneous GCU failsafe, 120-day power-cycle mandate.",
    "caveat": "The exact 32-bit/100Hz counter mechanism is a widely repeated technical inference, not confirmed by the FAA directive; presented as the leading theory.",
    "sharing_reason": "The fix for a billion-dollar jet is literally turning it off and on again."
  },
  "alternate_hook": "The FAA once ordered every Boeing 787 to be rebooted like a frozen laptop.",
